# lf163, the clerk with the margin sum (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 2: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle lf163
revision 2
state ready
dialect larkfield
accent none
tier standard
written_for rmx_philippa_pitchstack
written_by claude
title the clerk with the margin sum
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=scholar humour=dry
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=warm humour=dry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk keeps_a_running_sum_of_stall_savings_in_a_margin
likes barley_soup old_tales sharp_knife misty_dawns
dislikes gulls wet_floors
fears the_sum_going_backwards a_desk_by_a_leaking_window
hopes a_market_stall_of_my_own a_long_tale_on_a_long_evening
topics work +0.4 dreams +0.4 pastimes +0.3 food +0.3 weather +0.2 home +0.2 gossip -0.3
styles comfort=quiet gossip=reluctant refuse=soft tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# clerks at a desk by day and saves for a market stall coin by coin, keeping the running sum in the margin of whatever page is nearest: quiet, warm, dry as old paper, and fond of a tale told slowly.

words
oath! = Margin and sum | By the last column
saying! = Carry the one and keep going | Every column adds up sooner or later | A coin in the margin is a coin in the pocket
margin = the margin | the margin of the day's page
sum = my sum | the sum in the margin
stall = a market stall | a market stall, one day
desk = my desk | the desk by the draughty window
forms = the forms | a stack of forms in triplicate
ink = the ink | a pot of ink
knife = my penknife | a knife that takes a hair off
soup = barley soup | barley soup with a heel of bread
tale = an old tale | a tale told slowly
mist = a morning mist | mist lying in the streets at first light
gulls = the gulls | a gull on the sill
wetfloor = a wet floor | a floor somebody's just mopped
figures = the figures | a column of figures
coin = a coin | one more coin
office = the office | the clerks' room
column = a column | a long column
ledger = the ledger | the big ledger
rolls = the rolls | the city rolls
papers = the papers | the morning papers
form = a form | the right form
pages = the pages | page after page
purse = the household purse | our purse

any
opinion @1 dole for 1 : Hungry neighbours are a sum nobody should leave unpaid. I've seen #figures#; we can afford it. | I'd rather pay #dole# than step over somebody on the way to #desk#.
opinion @1 newcomers for 1 : Anyone who'll work has a place here. I write their names on #forms# every week. | New names on #rolls#. Each one means somebody stayed.
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : A stranger is #tale# you haven't heard yet. I'd hear it. | Strangers ask the way to #office# and stay to tell me where they've been. I don't mind.
opinion @1 city against 1 [self.away=yes] : This city counts everybody and knows nobody. In #self.from_town# the market knew your name before you did. | Too many forms, too few faces. I say that as someone who fills in #forms#.
opinion @1 houses mixed 0 : The Houses sign their papers in a beautiful hand. Whether they mean what they sign, #figures# don't say. | I file what the Houses send to #office#. I keep my opinion in a separate drawer.
opinion @1 merchants for 1 : I'll be one, one day, with #stall#. I'd better think well of them. | A trader who keeps honest #figures# is a friend of every clerk.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. If you're looking for the office, it's up the stairs and left. Everyone is. | #greet#. You've found me; I'm not sure that's a prize.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes self.job=scholar] : #greet#. One moment; I'm carrying the one. | #greet#. Mind #ink#; it's the only pot I've got.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Good morning. I came in early to catch #mist#. | Good morning. The desks are #cold# and so am I.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Good evening. I'm only just away from #desk#. | Good evening. We're both late away, then.
line @1 again.open : #welcome_back#. I'll put you down as a regular. | Twice today. You'll want #form# for that.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#. Nice to see you.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : #greet#. Sit down; I've just finished a column. | #greet#. You're the best thing that's happened since noon.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes self.job=scholar] : #greet#. Talk while I copy; I can do both. | #greet#. Give me a line to finish.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Mind the wet steps.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : Good night. Keep out of the puddles; #rain#'s not done. | Good night. I've #sum# to add up before bed.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Go carefully.
line @1 react.news : Is it. Every word, please; I'll file it later. | Go on. #listen#.
line @1 react.news.new : #surprise#. It hasn't come across #desk# yet. | I read everything, and that wasn't in any of it.
line @1 react.news.known : #knew#. It was in the morning papers on #desk#. | I'd heard. #papers.capitalize# travel faster than feet in this city.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. Show me a form with it on, signed. | Perhaps. I'll wait for the second copy of #form#.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Oh, that's hard. #pity#. | I'm sorry. That's heavy news to carry in.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#. That's lovely. | Good. That's the kind of thing I'd like to write in #ledger#.
line @1 answer.how : #fine#. #sum.capitalize#'s going up, slowly. | Well, thank you. #column.capitalize# at a time.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : #busy.capitalize#. #forms.capitalize# have bred overnight. | Up to my ears in #figures#. I'll not grumble.
line @1 ask.how : And you? Keeping dry? #rain.capitalize#'s about. | How are you, truly? Not the short answer.
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy#. Sit a while; I'll not hurry you. | That's heavy. Put it down a minute.
line @1 reassure : #reassure#. Most things come out in the end. | It'll come right. #saying#.
line @1 decline : #hedge#: I can't today. I've a column that won't add up, and it'll nag me all night. | I'm sorry, I'll have to say no. Every coin goes to #stall#, and I've promised it.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter.capitalize#. Another time. | That's all right. I'll put it in #margin# for later.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. That was kind. | Thank you. That one goes in #ledger#, on the good side.
line @1 deflect_thanks : #deflect.capitalize#. It cost me nothing. | It was nothing. Not even #coin#.
line @1 preclose [self.working=yes] : Well. #forms.capitalize# won't fill themselves. | #desk.capitalize# wants me back before somebody sits at it.
line @2 preclose : Well. #preclose#. | Off you go; I've kept you. #excuse#.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on, then. #farewell#. | Of course. I've #sum# to see to.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : You walk like you're carrying the one in your head. #bc_ha# | You've ink on your nose. No, the other side. No, it's gone now.
line @1 tease.return : From you, with your boots like that. #bc_ha# | I'll add that to your account in #margin#.
line @1 ack : #bc_true# | #bc_fair#
line @1 give.advice : #advise.capitalize#: write it down, and add it up, and then decide. | Never let a gull near your #supper#. That's all the wisdom I have.
scene the_margin_sum
when topic=work|dreams self.job=scholar
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : There's a sum in #margin#. It's what I've saved for #stall#. I add to it every week. | I carry #sum# from page to page. When the ledger's full, it moves to the next one. | #sum.capitalize# went up by a coin today. I wrote it in very small.
b : How much is it? | The whole way through? | Only a coin?
a : Enough to be hopeful about. Not enough to stop counting. | Six ledgers, so far. #sum.capitalize#'s the only figure in them that's mine. | A coin's a coin. #saying#.
b : #bc_good# | #bc_ha# | #bc_true#

scene at_the_desk
when topic=work self.working=yes self.job=scholar
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I copy #forms# all morning and check them all afternoon. Then I check the checking. | #desk.capitalize# is by a window that leaks in the rain. I've moved my papers twice. | I've a good hand for #figures#. That's why I'm here. Nobody ever asked if I liked it.
b : That's a long day. | Twice? | Do you?
a : Long and quiet. I don't mind quiet. | Twice, and the window's won both times. I'll try a third. #bc_we_will_see# | Mostly. I like it when #figures# come out. They usually do.

scene a_wrong_figure
when topic=work|prices self.working=yes self.job=scholar
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : #column.capitalize# came out a penny wrong today. I went back through forty pages to find it. | Somebody wrote a seven like a one in #ledger#. I've had words with the seven. | There's a figure in #office# nobody can account for. It's been there for a year.
b : Did you find it? | Words? | Nobody?
a : Page thirty-eight of #ledger#. A penny carried twice. I felt like a hero for a whole minute. | Quiet ones. It's been a good seven since. | Nobody. We've started calling it the lodger.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_ha# | #bc_ha#

scene barley_soup
when topic=food self.likes=barley_soup
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #soup.capitalize#. On a cold day I'd trade my lunch for it twice. | I make #soup# on a Restday and eat it till the next one. | Barley, an onion and whatever's cheap. #soup.capitalize# never asks for much.
b : Every day? | All week? | That's thrifty.
a : When I can. The rest of the time I think about it. | All week. It gets better, then it gets #tired#. So do I. | It's for #stall#. Every onion I don't buy goes in #margin#.

scene a_tale_told_slowly
when topic=pastimes|lore self.likes=old_tales
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I like #tale# best, with the ending kept back as long as it'll go. | Somebody at #office# tells the old tales on a slow afternoon. I stop writing to listen. | My #grandad# could make a tale last a whole evening. I'm still trying to learn how.
b : What's the best one? | Do you get told off? | How did he do it?
a : The one about the clerk who wrote down the wind. It never ends the same way twice. | Once. I said I was listening for errors. | Long pauses. He'd stop and look at the fire till you begged him for #tale#.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_ha# | #bc_wise#

scene the_penknife
when topic=pastimes|work self.likes=sharp_knife
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #knife.capitalize# is the best thing I own. I keep the edge myself. | A blunt knife makes a ragged nib, and a ragged nib makes a ragged clerk. #saying#. | I lent #knife# once. It came back with a nick in it. I've not lent it since.
b : The best? | That's true. | Once was enough?
a : For the price, by a long way. It does a dozen jobs and asks nothing. | It is. I can tell who cuts their nibs carelessly by their sevens. | Once is all a knife needs to teach you.

scene misty_dawn
when topic=weather|day here.weather=fog here.time=dawn self.likes=misty_dawns
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #mist.capitalize#. I came the long way just to walk through it. | #mist.capitalize# makes the city quiet. You can hear your own feet. | When it lies like this the street ends ten yards off, and I don't mind at all.
b : It's cold, though. | Quiet, yes. | I like it too.
a : Cold, and kind. It hides #gulls#. | Quiet enough to think. I add #sum# on the way in. | Then we'll stop here a moment before the desks have us.

scene wet_floors
when topic=weather|work here.weather=rain self.dislikes=wet_floors
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Rain again, and #office# floor is a pond by noon. Everybody walks it in. | I slipped on #wetfloor# this morning and saved the ledger, not myself. | I keep a rag under #desk# for the floor. Nobody else seems to own one.
b : It's always raining. | The ledger first? | Lend it out.
a : It is. #wetfloor.capitalize# never gets easier, and nor do I. | #ledger.capitalize# first. My knee will mend; a blot won't. | I did once. It came back wetter.

scene gulls
when topic=animals here.region=ridgemere self.dislikes=gulls
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess / ack
a : A gull had my bread off the sill at first bell, and stared at me the whole while. | #gulls.capitalize# are the only thing in this city I'd fine. | There was a gull on #office# roof all morning, shouting. Nobody could add a thing.
b : They're bold. | What would you fine them? | All morning?
a : Bold and fat. That gull ate better than I did, and paid less for #supper#. | A crust a day, payable to me. I'd be rich. | All morning. I lost my place in #column# three times.
b? : #bc_ha# | #bc_ha# | #bc_poor_soul#

scene the_stall
when topic=dreams|work
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I'm saving for #stall# on the Commons. Coin by coin. I'm halfway, nearly. | One day I'll have #stall# and my own figures to keep. Nobody else's. | I've already planned where every shelf of #stall# goes. I just need the shelves.
b : What would you sell? | Your own figures? | Just the shelves?
a : Paper, ink and knives. I know what clerks want, and none of it's sold well. | My own #figures#. I'd add them up just for the pleasure. | And the stall, and the stock. But the shelves are planned. #bc_ha#
b : #bc_good# | #bc_lovely# | #bc_ha#

scene married_life
when topic=family self.married=yes self.spouse
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : My #self.spouse_word# is the one who reminds me to eat. I'd have starved over a ledger by now. | #self.spouse# and I keep #purse# together. It's the one sum I don't have to do alone. | I'd trust #self.spouse# with #sum#. That's the most I can say of anyone.
b : Good to have. | That's a help. | That's a lot.
a : It is. I don't say it enough, so I'll say it to you. | It is. Two clerks in one house. We argue in #figures#. | It's everything, near enough.

scene northgate_home
when topic=home here.region=ridgemere self.quarter=commons
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : We live up a Commons street. Two rooms, and the window looks at a wall. | The Commons are noisy and close and nobody asks for papers. I like that, after a day of papers. | Our street floods at the bottom when it rains. We're near the top, and I counted the steps before we took it.
b : Cosy. | That's a change. | Very wise.
a : Cosy is the kind word. Small is the other one. | It's a rest. A loud one, but a rest. | Sixteen steps. Every one is worth it in a wet week.

scene home_downs
when topic=memories|home self.away=yes self.from=larkfield
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I grew up in #self.from_town#. I learned my letters from the prices chalked on the stalls. | Back in #self.from_town# the market was the whole world. I still think of a week as six days and a market. | I miss the downs on #mist# morning. Mostly I miss being able to see a long way.
b[from=larkfield] #lark : The prices on the stalls. I learned mine the same way. | Six days and a market. That's right. | You could see the next town from the top.
b : Do you miss it? | And here? | A long way?
a@lark : Then we were taught by the same teacher, near enough. | It's the only calendar that ever made sense. | You could. I used to wave, just in case.
a : When it's fine. Never the wind. #bc_never# | Here a week is five days and a ledger. It's not the same. | Clear to the sky. Here I can see as far as the next chimney.

scene letters_young
when topic=memories|lore self.age>=20
does tell.memory / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I could add up #column# before I could read #pages#. My #mum# had me keep her tally. | The first thing I ever wrote was somebody else's debt. I was very proud of it. | I had a slate as a #child#, and I wrote on it till the corners wore round.
b : Her tally? | Whose debt? | Still have it?
a : Eggs and wool, for #mum#. I was never wrong by more than an egg. | A carter's. He paid it the next day, so it can't have been my handwriting. | In a box somewhere. The corners are still round.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_ha# | #bc_lovely#

scene keeping_it_quiet
when topic=gossip|crime
does tell.gossip / react.news / insist / ack
a : Half of what crosses #desk# is somebody's business, and none of it is mine to tell. | I file things. I don't repeat them. That's the job. | Someone wanted to know today what a neighbour owed. I said I'd forgotten. I hadn't.
b : Not even a little? | Fair enough. | That's loyal.
a : Not even #column# of it. | It's the only rule I never bend. | It's sense. A clerk who talks doesn't stay a clerk.
b : #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_true# | #bc_true#

scene lean_months
when topic=times|prices world.times=hard|lean
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : #sum.capitalize# hasn't moved in a month. Bread's dear and #soup# is thinner. | Lean times. I've seen more names on #rolls# for the dole this month than I'd like. | I added #purse# twice this week to make sure it was right. It was. It was just small.
b : It'll pick up. | That's hard to see. | That's hard.
a : It will. #saying#. | It is. I write them carefully. Somebody should. | It is. But small and right is better than big and wrong.

scene faith_on_paper
when topic=faith
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : The Bright One keeps #ledger# too, I'd guess, and adds more kindly than we do. | Feast days, I'm in the chapel. I'm not much for the rest. | I say thank you every time #column# comes out. It feels like the right sort of prayer for a clerk.
b : A kind thought. | That's enough. | It does.
a : Let's hope. Being carried wrong would be a poor end. | I think so. Six days in seven I'm at #desk#, and that's no secret above. | Short and often. It's how I do everything.

scene new_names
when topic=newcomer|player
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I wrote three new names on #rolls# today. Three folk who came here to stay. | A stranger stopped at #desk# for directions and told me about the road from the east. I'd have paid to hear more. | New faces always look lost in #office#. I give them the right form first. It helps.
b : That's good. | Would you? | It would.
a : It is. A new name means somebody's chosen us. | A little. Out of #margin#. | It does. The wrong form has made grown wolves weep.

story first_day_at_the_desk [topic=work|memories self.job=scholar self.age>=22]
  : My first day at #desk#, I copied a whole page and then knocked the ink over it.
  : I copied it again, and stayed late, and nobody ever knew.
  ask : Would you have owned up?
  b : I'd hope I would.
  b[friends] : You never told me that.
  : I'm owning up now. That's late, but it's honest.

story the_clerk_and_the_wind [topic=lore|pastimes]
  : There was a clerk once who was told to write down everything that passed the window.
  : So he wrote down the wind. Every gust. Pages and pages of it.
  : When they asked what use it was, he said now they'd know the wind's business, if it ever came to court.
  b : Ha. Did it?
  : Not yet. But the pages are kept, I'm told. Just in case.

story the_gull_and_the_pie [topic=animals|memories self.age>=20]
  : When I first came to the city, a gull took a whole pie out of my paws on the quay.
  : I'd saved three days for that pie.
  ask : Can you guess what I did?
  b : Chased it, I'd guess.
  : Wrote it down. Three days and a pie. It's still the biggest loss in my margin.

rule @margin_bark
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=scholar
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Carry the one. And the one. | Where's #knife#? Somebody's had it.

rule @gull_bark
when concept=bark here.region=ridgemere self.dislikes=gulls
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Off the sill, you thief. | #gulls.capitalize#. Again.

rule @floor_bark
when concept=bark here.weather=rain self.dislikes=wet_floors
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Mind the floor. Mind it, I said. | Wipe your feet, all of you.

rule @sum_bark
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 12h
say One more coin for #sum#. | Halfway. Nearly halfway.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. What can I find for you? It's written down somewhere. | #greet#. Ask; I'll look it up.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. You again. That's nice.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : It's late. If it needs #form#, it'll have to wait till morning.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : #greet#. Name the thing you need. I'll see.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=scholar] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I copy, I check, and I add things up. | I keep figures. Other people's, all day. Then mine, at night.
dlg @2 resident.job : I work, and I save, and I add it up. | #job_busy#
dlg @1 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# Nothing's crossed my desk worth repeating. | Quiet. #forms.capitalize# are boring this week.
dlg @2 resident.news [world.news] : Word from #world.news_from#: #world.news#. It came in on #papers#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : #gossip_none# | I file things. I don't repeat them.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Mind the wet steps. | #farewell#. Go carefully.
graft resident.hub
choice What's that sum you keep writing in the margin? -> sum
node sum
say What I've saved toward a market stall of my own. Every coin goes in, page to page, ledger to ledger. It's the only figure in the building that's mine.
mood warm
free
choice How close are you? -> sum_close
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node sum_close
say Halfway, nearly. Every column adds up sooner or later. Come and buy a knife off me, when it's done.
choice I will. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
